$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Preparation of propionic
acid-(R)-3-iodoethyl-1-phenethylbut-3-enyl ester. To a stirring solution
of the ester (116.9 mg, 0.416 mmol, 1.00 eq) and acetone (4.2 mL, 0.10 M)
in a 25 mL round-bottom flask at room temperature was added NaI (1.25 g,
8.32 mmol, 20 eq). The mixture was kept at room temperature in the dark
for 24 h and then diluted with Et2O (15 mL). The mixture was filtered
through a plug of Celite®, the filtrate was diluted with Et2O (50 mL) and
filtered through the same plug of Celite®. The filtrate was concentrated
under reduced pressure and the residue was purified by flash
chromatography on a 1.5 x 18 cm silica gel column eluting with a solvent
gradient of 2.5% (100 mL) through 5% EtOAc/hexanes (100 mL). The eluant
was collected in 10 mL portions and the product containing fractions (6
to 12) were combined and concentrated. 3-benzyloxy-propionic acid
(R)-3-iodomethyl-1-phenethyl-but-3-enyl ester as a clear colorless oil,
yield 173 mg, 0.362 mmol, 100%. Rf 0.65 (25% EtOAc/hexanes); [α]20D +14.1
(c = 1.075, CHCl3); 500 MHz 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 7.35 - 7.34 (m, 4H), 7.32
-7.28 (m, 3H), 7.22 - 7.17 (m, 3H), 5.27 (s, 1H), 5.15 (dddd, J = 7.9,
7.9, 4.7, 4.7 Hz, 1H), 4.94 (s, 1H), 4.55 (s, 2H), 3.99 (d, J = 9.4 Hz,
1H), 3.91 (d, J = 9.4 Hz, 1H), 3.78 - 3.75 (m, 2H), 2.73 - 2.60 (m, 5H),
2.46 (dd, J = 14.8, 8.4 Hz, 1H), 1.96 - 1.90 (m, 2H); 125 MHz 13C NMR
(CDCl3) δ 171.4, 142.8, 141.5, 138.2, 128.6 (2), 128.6 (2), 128.5 (2),
127.9 (3), 126.2, 117.1, 73.3, 71.8, 65.9, 39.3, 36.0, 35.6, 31.9, 10.7;
125 MHz DEPT (CDCl3) δ CH2: 117.1, 73.3, 65.9, 39.3, 36.0, 35.6, 32.0,
10.7. CH: 128.7 (2), 128.6 (2), 128.5 (2), 127.9 (3), 126.2, 71.8. C:
171.4, 142.8, 141.5, 138.2; IR (neat) 3084, 3062, 3027, 2952, 2922, 2863,
1732, 1635, 1603, 1496, 1454, 1431, 1365, 1252, 1181, 1104, 1070, 1028,
910, 740, 699 cm-1; Anal. Calcd for C23H27IO3: C, 57.75; H, 5.69. Found:
C, 58.14; H, 5.58.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM in the dark
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
