$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Typical Procedures for F/I exchange of secondary and tertiary alkyl
fluorides. A typical procedure is given for the synthesis of 2d. To a
hexane (2.5 mL) were added Et3Al (1.0 M in hexane, 0.5 mL, 0.5 mmol) and
CH2I2 (80 μl, 2 mmol), then the reaction mixture was stirred for 90 min.
(Active species was generated and 1-iodoethane was formed as byproduct.)
After the reaction mixture was cooled to-30 °C, 2-fluorododecane 2a (94
mg, 0.5 mmol) was added and stirred for 30 min at the same temperature.
The reaction was quenched with 3 M aqueous HCl solution slowly and
extracted with hexane. The organic phase was filtered through a short pad
of silica gel. The solvents and volatile compounds were removed under
reduced pressure. A mixture of 2-iodododecane 2d and 2-dodecene. NMR
yield: 91%. CAS Registry Number [68453-80-5]. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ
0.88 (t, J = 6.9 Hz, 3H), 1.28-1.32 (m, 16H), 1.55-1.64 (m, 1H),
1.78-1.88 (m, 1H), 1.91 (d, J = 7.1 Hz, 3H), 4.13-4.22 (m, 1H). 13C{1H}
NMR (101 MHz, CDCl3): δ 14.1, 22.7, 28.7, 28.9, 29.3, 29.4, 29.6 (2C),
29.7, 30.7, 31.9, 42.9.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Halogen Exchange Reaction of Aliphatic Fluorine Compounds with Organic
Halides as Halogen Source
