$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Typical procedure for F/Br exchange of secondary and tertiary alkyl
fluorides. A typical procedure is given for the synthesis of 2c. To a
suspension of Cp2TiBr2 (6.2 mg, 0.025 mmol) in hexane (4 mL) was added
Et3Al (1.0 M in hexane, 0.5 mL, 0.5 mmol) dropwise at 0 ºC, and the
mixture was stirred for 30 min at the same temperature, then warm up to
room temperature. After the mixture was stirred for 30 min, CH2Br2 (70
μL, 1 mmol) was added to the blue solution. 2-Fluorooctane 2a (94 mg, 0.5
mmol) in hexane (5 mL) was added dropwise and stirred for 30 min. The
reaction was quenched with 3 M aqueous HCl solution slowly and extracted
with hexane. The organic phase was filtered through a short pad of silica
gel. The solvents and volatile compounds were removed under reduced
pressure. 2-bromoctane 2c as colorless oil (124 mg, yield 99%).
2-Bromododecane (2c). Isolated yield: 99%. CAS Registry Number
[13187-99-0]. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 0.88 (t, J = 6.9 Hz, 3H),
1.28-1.32 (m, 16H), 1.70 (d, J = 6.6 Hz, 3H), 1.73-1.87 (m, 2H),
4.08-4.16 (m, 1H). 13C{1H} NMR (101 MHz, CDCl3): δ 14.1, 22.7, 26.4,
27.8, 29.0, 29.3, 29.5, 29.6 (2C), 31.9, 41.2, 51.9.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Halogen Exchange Reaction of Aliphatic Fluorine Compounds with Organic
Halides as Halogen Source
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Mizukami, Yuki; Song, Zhiyi; Takahashi, Tamotsu
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2015), 17(24), 5942-5945

