$DATUM Typical procedure for F/I exchange of primary alkyl fluorides. A typical
procedure is given for the synthesis of 1d. To a hexane (5 mL) was added
Et3Al (1.0 M in hexane, 1 mL, 1 mmol), and the mixture was cooled to-40
°C. CH2I2 (0.16 mL, 2 mmol) and 1-Fluorooctane 1a (0.16 mL, 1 mmol) were
added successively and the reaction mixture was slowly warmed up to room
temperature by removing the cooling bath. After stirring 24 h, the
reaction was quenched with 3 M aqueous HCl solution slowly and extracted
with hexane. The organic phase was filtered through a short pad of silica
gel. The solvents and volatile compounds were removed under reduced
pressure. 1-iodooctane 1d as colorless oil (120 mg, yield 99%). CAS
Registry Number [629-27-6]. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 0.88 (t, J = 6.9
Hz, 3H), 1.28-1.32 (br, 8H), 1.36-1.41 (m, 2H) 1.78-1.85 (m, 2H), 3.17
(t, J = 7.3 Hz, 2H). 13C{1H} NMR (101 MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.26, 14.1, 22.6,
28.5, 29.1, 30.5, 31.7, 33.5.
