$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Typical procedure for F/Cl and F/Br exchange of primary alkyl fluorides.
A typical procedure is given for the synthesis of 1b. To a suspension of
Cp2TiCl2 (7.5 mg, 0.03 mmol) in hexane (5 mL) was added i Bu3Al (1.0 M in
hexane, 1 mL, 1 mmol) dropwise at 0 ºC, and the mixture was stirred for
30 min at the same temperature, then warm up to room temperature. After
the mixture was stirred for 30 min, CH2Cl2 (0.13 mL, 2 mmol) and
1-fluorooctane 1a (0.16 mL, 1 mmol) were added to the blue solution
successively and stirred for 24 h. The reaction was quenched with 3 M
aqueous HCl solution slowly and extracted with hexane. The organic phase
was filtered through a short pad of silica gel. The solvents and volatile
compounds were removed under reduced pressure. 1-chlorooctane 1b as
colorless oil (148 mg, yield 99%). CAS Registry Number [111-85-3]. 1H NMR
(400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 0.88 (t, J = 6.9 Hz, 3H), 1.28-1.32 (m, 8H) 1.39-1.46
(m, 2H), 1.72-1.80 (m, 2H), 3.53 (t, J = 6.8 Hz, 2H). 13C{1H} NMR (101
MHz, CDCl3): δ 14.1, 22.6, 26.9, 28.9, 29.1, 31.7, 32.7, 45.2.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM optimized on catalyst, reagent, optimization study
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Halogen Exchange Reaction of Aliphatic Fluorine Compounds with Organic
Halides as Halogen Source
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
