$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for Iodide Displacement under Liquid-Liquid Conditions.
A mixture of 1-bromooctane (200 mg, 1.0 mmol), potassium iodide (840 mg,
5.0 mmol), biphenyl (154 mg, 1.0 mmol), benzotrifluoride (4 mL), water (2
mL), and the appropriate dialkyl-4,13-diaza-18-crown-6 ether (0.02 mmol)
was refluxed at 110 °C for 24 h. After cooling to room temperature, the
organic phase was filtered through silica gel using benzotrifluoride as
eluant. A sample of the collected solution was analyzed by gas
chromatography to determine the yield of product using biphenyl as the
internal standard (115 °C for 3 min followed by 45 °C min-1 ramp to 195
°C, held for 1 min. Injector: 300 °C, detector: 300 °C. Rt 2.13 min
(1-bromooctane), 2.85 min (1-iodooctane), 4.05 min (biphenyl)).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM other phase-transfer catalysts gave similar or lower yields
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Perfluoroalkylated 4,13-Diaza-18-Crown-6 Ethers: Synthesis,
Phase-Transfer Catalysis, and Recycling Studies
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Stuart, Alison M.; Vidal, Jose A.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2007), 72(10), 3735-3740

