$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of propionic acid-(R)-3-iodoethyl-1-phenethylbut-3-enyl
ester. To a stirring solution of the ester (116.9 mg, 0.416 mmol, 1.00
eq) and acetone (4.2 mL, 0.10 M) in a 25 mL round-bottom flask at room
temperature was added NaI (1.25 g, 8.32 mmol, 20 eq). The mixture was
kept at room temperature in the dark for 24 h and then diluted with Et2O
(15 mL). The mixture was filtered through a plug of Celite®, the filtrate
was diluted with Et2O (50 mL) and filtered through the same plug of
Celite®. The filtrate was concentrated under reduced pressure and the
residue was purified by flash chromatography on a 1.5 x 18 cm silica gel
column eluting with a solvent gradient of 2.5% (100 mL) through 5%
EtOAc/hexanes (100 mL). The eluant was collected in 10 mL portions and
the product containing fractions (6 to 12) were combined and
concentrated. Iodide as a clear slightly yellow oil, yield 145 mg, 0.390
mmol, 94%. Rf 0.68 (25% EtOAc/hexanes); [α]20D +22.9 (c = 1.015, CHCl3);
500 MHz 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 7.32 - 7.18 (m, 5H), 5.30 (s, 1H), 5.14 - 5.09
(m, 1H), 4.95 (s, 1H), 4.02 (d, J = 9.4 Hz, 1H), 3.93 (d, J = 9.4 Hz,
1H), 2.73 - 2.63 (m, 3H), 2.43 (dd, J = 14.6, 8.6 Hz, 1H), 2.31 (q, J =
7.7 Hz, 2H), 1.98 - 1.86 (m, 2H), 1.15 (t, J = 7.7 Hz, 3H); 125 MHz 13C
NMR (CDCl3) δ 174.3, 142.9, 141.5, 128.7 (2), 128.5 (2), 126.2, 117.0,
71.3, 39.4, 36.1, 32.1, 28.0, 10.6, 9.5; 125 MHz DEPT (CDCl3) δ CH3: 9.5.
CH2: 117.1, 39.5, 36.1, 32.1, 28.0, 10.6. CH: 128.7 (2), 128.5 (2),
126.3, 71.4. C: 174.3, 142.9, 141.5; IR (neat) 3083, 3026, 2978, 2940,
2861, 1732, 1634, 1602, 1495, 1454, 1432, 1273, 1185, 1080, 1028, 909,
748, 699 cm-1; Anal. Calcd for C16H21IO2: C, 51.63; H, 5.69. Found: C,
51.67; H, 5.71.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
