$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM The typical experimental procedure is as follows:
p-fluorobenzotrifluoride (1.07 g, 6.5 mmol) and carbon tetrachloride (5
mL) were added to a flask with a magnetic stir bar. The flask was
evacuated and backfilled with argon three times and then left under argon
atmosphere. Subsequently, boron tribromide (1.95 g, 7.8 mmol) was added
via a syringe. The mixture was stirred at room temperature for 36 h,
slowly changing from yellow to amber in color. Then, the reaction was
stopped by an addition of 15 mL of ice water. The resulting mixture was
extracted with CH2Cl2 (3 x 10 mL). The combined organic layer was washed
with ice water (3 x 5 mL) and dried over anhydrous CaCl2. After
evaporating the solvent, the crude product was purified by flash
chromatography (SiO2), and eluted with ethyl acetate/petroleum ether (Φr
= 2 : 98) to give p-fluorobenzotribromide. Compound I, yield 2.08 g, 92%.
Formula: C7H4Br3F; Mr: 346.82; wi(calc.)/%: C 24.24, H 1.16; wi(found)/%:
C 24.20, H 1.20. 1H NMR (CDCl3), δ: 7.07 (d, 2H, Ph), 8.02 (d, 2H, Ph)13C
NMR (CDCl3), δ: 34.13 (CBr3), 114.77 (2C, 2JCF = 22.2 Hz, Ph), 128.76
(2C, 3JCF = 8.7 Hz, Ph),143.20 (1C, 4JCF = 3.4 Hz, Ph), 163.11 (1C, 1JCF
= 250.8 Hz, Ph) MS, m/z (Ir/%): 346 (53), 348 (51) (M+).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM mechanism studied
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Mild and efficient conversion of trifluoromethylarenes into
tribromomethylarenes using boron tribromide
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Chen, Hongbiao; Yin, Jianxiang; Lin, Yuanbin
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Chemical Papers (2009), 63(1), 92-96

