$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: The typical experimental procedure is as
follows: p-fluorobenzotrifluoride (1.07 g, 6.5 mmol) and carbon
tetrachloride (5 mL) were added to a flask with a magnetic stir bar. The
flask was evacuated and backfilled with argon three times and then left
under argon atmosphere. Subsequently, boron tribromide (1.95 g, 7.8 mmol)
was added via a syringe. The mixture was stirred at room temperature for
36 h, slowly changing from yellow to amber in color. Then, the reaction
was stopped by an addition of 15 mL of ice water. The resulting mixture
was extracted with CH2Cl2 (3 x 10 mL). The combined organic layer was
washed with ice water (3 x 5 mL) and dried over anhydrous CaCl2. After
evaporating the solvent, the crude product was purified by flash
chromatography (SiO2), and eluted with ethyl acetate/petroleum ether (Φr
= 2 : 98) to give p-fluorobenzotribromide. Compound VIII, yield 85%.
Formula: C8H4Br6; Mr: 579.54; wi(calc.)/%: C 16.58, H 0.70; wi(found)/%:
C 16.61, H 0.68. M.p./°C: 85-86 (lit. 85-87). 1H NMR (CDCl3), δ: 7.46 (s,
1H, Ph), 7.98 (d, 2H, Ph), 8.28 (t, 1H, Ph) 13C NMR (CDCl3), δ: 34.31
(2C, CBr3), 124.85 (1C, Ph), 128.14 (3C, Ph), 146.77 (2C, Ph) MS, m/z
(Ir/%): 580 (66) (M+).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM mechanism studied
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Mild and efficient conversion of trifluoromethylarenes into
tribromomethylarenes using boron tribromide
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Chen, Hongbiao; Yin, Jianxiang; Lin, Yuanbin
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Chemical Papers (2009), 63(1), 92-96

