$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Reaction of octylbromide with potassium iodide
in the solid-liquid condition The cross-linked copolymer (0.50 g),
octylbromide (0.01 mol, 1.93 g), KI (0.05 mol, 8.30 g), and acetonitrile
(10 mL) were charged in a round bottomed flask. Then, the reaction
mixture was stirred and refluxed for 12 h. After this time, the copolymer
was recovered by filtration and yield of the reaction was obtained by GC
analysis. 2,4-Dinitro-chlorobenzene, Catalyst copolymer 4, yield 64%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM phase transfer catalysis, catalyst recyclable
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis and applications of cross-linked poly(diallyldimethyl ammonium
chloride) and its derivative copolymers as efficient phase transfer
catalyst for nucleophilic substitution reactions
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Mahdavi, Hossein; Mahmoudian, Mahdi
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Chinese Journal of Polymer Science (2011), 29(2), 165-172

