$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical procedure for F/Cl and F/Br exchange
of primary alkyl fluorides. A typical procedure is given for the
synthesis of 1b. To a suspension of Cp2TiCl2 (7.5 mg, 0.03 mmol) in
hexane (5 mL) was added i Bu3Al (1.0 M in hexane, 1 mL, 1 mmol) dropwise
at 0 ºC, and the mixture was stirred for 30 min at the same temperature,
then warm up to room temperature. After the mixture was stirred for 30
min, CH2Cl2 (0.13 mL, 2 mmol) and 1-fluorooctane 1a (0.16 mL, 1 mmol)
were added to the blue solution successively and stirred for 24 h. The
reaction was quenched with 3 M aqueous HCl solution slowly and extracted
with hexane. The organic phase was filtered through a short pad of silica
gel. The solvents and volatile compounds were removed under reduced
pressure. Bromocyclohexane (3c). The compound 3c was prepared with
Cp2TiBr2 (10.1 mg, 0.03 mmol), Et3Al (1.0 M in hexane, 1 mL, 1 mmol),
CH2Br2 (0.14 mL, 2 mmol) and fluorocyclohexane 3a (0.11 mL, 1 mmol). The
reaction gave a mixture of bromocyclohexane and elimination side product
(cyclohexene). NMR yield: 78%. CAS Registry Number [108-85-0]. 1H NMR
(400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 1.32-1.43 (m, 3H), 1.52-1.61 (m, 1H), 1.72-1.87 (m,
4H), 2.12-2.19 (m, 2H), 4.16-4.23 (m, 1H). 13C{1H} NMR (101 MHz, CDCl3):
δ 25.1, 25.9, 37.6, 53.6.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Halogen Exchange Reaction of Aliphatic Fluorine Compounds with Organic
Halides as Halogen Source
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Mizukami, Yuki; Song, Zhiyi; Takahashi, Tamotsu
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2015), 17(24), 5942-5945

