$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical Procedures for F/I exchange of
secondary and tertiary alkyl fluorides. A typical procedure is given for
the synthesis of 2d. To a hexane (2.5 mL) were added Et3Al (1.0 M in
hexane, 0.5 mL, 0.5 mmol) and CH2I2 (80 μl, 2 mmol), then the reaction
mixture was stirred for 90 min. (Active species was generated and
1-iodoethane was formed as byproduct.) After the reaction mixture was
cooled to-30 °C, 2-fluorododecane 2a (94 mg, 0.5 mmol) was added and
stirred for 30 min at the same temperature. The reaction was quenched
with 3 M aqueous HCl solution slowly and extracted with hexane. The
organic phase was filtered through a short pad of silica gel. The
solvents and volatile compounds were removed under reduced pressure.
Iodocyclohexane (3d). The compound 3d was prepared with Et3Al (1.0 M in
hexane, 1 mL, 1 mmol), CH2I2 (0.16 mL, 2 mmol) and fluorocyclohexane 3a
(0.11 mL, 1 mmol). The reaction gave a mixture of iodocyclohexane 3d and
elimination side product (cyclohexene). NMR yield: 94%. CAS Registry
Number [626-62-0]. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 1.35-1.44 (m, 3H),
1.61-1.70 (m, 3H), 1.91-2.01 (m, 2H), 2.11-2.19 (m, 2H), 4.32-4.39 (m,
1H). 13C{1H} NMR (101 MHz, CDCl3): δ 25.2, 27.3, 32.8, 39.6.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM cyclohexene as a minor byproduct
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Halogen Exchange Reaction of Aliphatic Fluorine Compounds with Organic
Halides as Halogen Source
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Mizukami, Yuki; Song, Zhiyi; Takahashi, Tamotsu
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2015), 17(24), 5942-5945

